                     "content" : [
                        {
                           "content" : [
                              {
                                 "text" : " @todo   Consider adding 'max-size' feature to Q. With this set, attempt to add item past",
                                 "type" : "text"
                              }
                           ],
                           "type" : "codeBlock"
                        }
                     ],
                     "type" : "listItem"
                  },
                  {
                     "content" : [
                        {
                           "content" : [
                              {
                                 "text" : "         max size would throw. This can be handy with stuff like blocking q? and probably",
                                 "type" : "text"
                              }
                           ],
                           "type" : "codeBlock"
                        }
                     ],
                     "type" : "listItem"
                  },
                  {
                     "content" : [
                        {
                           "content" : [
                              {
                                 "text" : "         other cases as well (when you don't want q to grow indefinitely).",
                                 "type" : "text"
                              }
                           ],
                           "type" : "codeBlock"
                        }
                     ],
                     "type" : "listItem"
                  },
                  {
                     "content" : [
                        {
                           "type" : "paragraph"
                        }
                     ],
                     "type" : "listItem"
                  }
               ],
               "type" : "bulletList"
            },
            {
               "content" : [
                  {
                     "text" : "Ø  Two cases – max-size where you want to fail when you get too large (that’s why I outlined in that tod.",
                     "type" : "text"
                  }
               ],
               "type" : "paragraph"
            },
            {
               "content" : [
                  {
                     "text" : "Ø  But other interesting case John raised – was a by-design circular queue, where you really just intend it to be OK to overflow the quque. A good example of this is for impmemting “RECENT HISOTRY’ You want old stuff to run off the end, but newer stuff at the head of the q. MAYBE QUEUE is the wrong concept. Maybe call it ‘History. You add stuff to it, and old stuff rolls off the end. And its intended to be used to statistics like  keep track of Q1 (upper quartile) entries, or maybe good enough to just keep last n, so we can run separate algorithm on the list. Maybe want this to be separate from Q cuz you want to be able to array index (often) to do some kinds of history.",
                     "type" : "text"
                  }
               ],
               "type" : "paragraph"
            },
            {
               "type" : "paragraph"
            },
            {
               "content" : [
                  {
                     "text" : " ",
                     "type" : "text"
                  }
               ],
               "type" : "paragraph"
            },
            {
               "content" : [
                  {
                     "text" : "“CappedSizeQueue” – and then policy in CTOR, if you throw or remove – or maybe handler arg in CTOR – which can be removelast or throw. But maybe better to have ‘history’ class since it would allow array indexing?",
                     "type" : "text"
                  }
               ],
               "type" : "paragraph"
            },
            {
               "content" : [
                  {
                     "text" : " ",
                     "type" : "text"
                  }
               ],
               "type" : "paragraph"
            }
         ],
